4. How do we interpret skewness?
    Skewness measures the asymmetry of a distribution.

A rough practical rule:

        Skewness	    Interpretation

        ~0	            Approximately symmetric
        0 to 0.5	    Low positive skew
        0.5 to 1	    Moderate positive skew
        > 1	            High positive skew
        < -1	        High negative skew

        between −0.5 and 0.5	~symmetric	no transform needed
        between ±0.5 and ±1.0	moderately skewed	optional, test both
        beyond ±1.0	            highly skewed	apply log1p

These are rules of thumb, not strict mathematical thresholds.
